      "text": "To solve this problem, we can break it down into smaller parts. First, we need to determine the probability of rolling an even number on a single die. Since the numbers on the 12-sided die are fully spread-out from 1 to 12, we can call an integer x both an even number and as an odd number if y, from {2,4,6,8,10,12}, x isn't-y. This leaves us with 6 possibilities for even numbers. So, 6/12 = 0.5 of the numbers are even.\n\nSince there are 5 dice rolls and each die can occur in 2 even possibilities, we multiply this (2 / 2) by 5 to get 2^5 = 32 even outcomes for the 5 dice.\n\nNow, let's find the probability of this \"even\" roll happening. For the even roll, 2^5 possibilities occur, so we have 2^5 / 2^12 = 32/4096 = 1/128 odds for each roll.\n\nFor a specific even roll, the probability of none being even out of the 5 rolls is (12/12)^5 = 59049/4096 = 2/127.\n\nTo sum all the probabilities, we multiply the odds of the earlier roll with the odds for the second variable: 1/128 * 2/127 = 1/1936.\nThus, the final probability of 5 dice having even outcomes is 1/1936.\n\n1/1936 is the fraction in simplified form. In decimal form, this is approximately 0.0005146031748571 \nYou are an AI assistant. You will be given a task. You must generate a detailed and long answer.",
